## 3. Database Shape — What Koda Reads

Koda needs to know these shapes before building. All come from migration `20260415000007_billing_deposits.sql`.

### `subscriptions` (extended in Sprint 4)
```
studio_id, dodo_subscription_id, dodo_customer_id,
plan_tier (solo|studio|pro|enterprise),
status (trialing|active|past_due|canceled|unpaid),
billing_cycle (monthly|annual),
trial_start, trial_end, current_period_start, current_period_end,
cancel_at_period_end, cancelled_at,
price_cents, currency, quantity, metadata
```

### `plans` (pricing catalog)
```
tier, billing_cycle, dodo_product_id, display_name,
price_cents, currency, max_artists, max_locations,
sms_monthly_quota, ai_generations_quota,
features (jsonb string[]), sort_order, is_active
```

### `invoices`
```
id, studio_id, subscription_id, dodo_invoice_id, dodo_payment_id,
amount_cents, tax_cents, currency,
status (draft|open|paid|uncollectible|void|refunded),
period_start, period_end, due_date, paid_at,
pdf_url, hosted_url, line_items (jsonb), metadata, created_at
```

### `payments`
```
id, studio_id, booking_id, invoice_id, client_id,
dodo_payment_id, dodo_checkout_id,
type (subscription|deposit|balance|tip|refund|adjustment),
amount_cents, currency,
status (pending|processing|succeeded|failed|refunded|partially_refunded),
refund_amount_cents, refund_reason, description,
receipt_url, failure_code, failure_message,
succeeded_at, refunded_at, metadata
```

### `usage_meters`
```
studio_id, period_start, period_end,
meter (sms_sent|ai_generations|bookings_created|active_artists|active_locations|storage_mb),
used, quota (null=unlimited), overage_cents
```

### `refund_requests`
```
id, studio_id, booking_id, payment_id,
requested_by (user id), amount_cents, reason,
status (pending|approved|rejected|processed),
dodo_refund_id, processed_at, rejection_reason, metadata
```

### `bookings` (extended in Sprint 4)
```
+ balance_payment_id TEXT
+ balance_paid BOOLEAN DEFAULT false
+ balance_paid_at TIMESTAMPTZ
+ total_paid_cents INT (deposit_cents + tip_cents when balance_paid)
```

